clearHolderT -- SEQ 577 (Tony, 2026-11-09): the old road's holder read-through, PINNED AS TRIPWIRES, not born red. The cure is
parked (R0). Every row reads TODAY's value; the rule's answer (SEQ 561 R3: clear(h) empties the holder, clear(*h) the target,
argument the one exception, and a bare name means the holder) is named beside it in pop.sh. A row that moves is a finding.

THE MECHANISM (docs/clearHolderRecon.md, SEQ 577): getLabelGroup (GroupItem.twk:929-930) walks group links to the first node that
is not a group. A call's argument is fetched through it (aCTionParens), so a holder that already holds a group when the statement is
BUILT is walked through to its target; built before the bind, the walk stops at the holder. Top-level statements are always built
after their binds.

One process, rows prefixed CH. Each print carries the target's value then the holder's isGrouP after the clear.
  OT-H   top level clear(h)                                    today: target emptied, holder kept   rule: holder emptied
  X1     bound in an action, cleared at top                    today: target emptied               rule: holder emptied
  X2     bound at top, cleared in an action built after it     today: target emptied               rule: holder emptied
  Z2     an action first built after the bind                  today: target emptied               rule: holder emptied
  OT-AH  clear(argument), a holder passed from the top level   today: target emptied               rule: holder emptied
  NA-AH  the same, the action built on the new road            today: target emptied (the CALL is old road)  rule: holder
  TA     addrOf(target) then addrOf(holder) at top level       today: the same body                rule: different bodies
  TS     a user action's argument, a holder passed at top      today: tagged as the target         rule: the holder
  JC-H   a compiled action (jitter;) built after the bind      today: target emptied               rule: holder emptied
  K1     control: top level clear(*h)                          today and rule: target emptied
  K2     control: := and clear in the same action              today and rule: holder emptied
